{"t":"Bakragore's Burden","s":"bakragore-s-burden-a59ad","k":"outro","i":"assets/wiki/The_Essence_of_Murcion_c56c4c.gif","q":1,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-twbox2 pi-layout-default\" role=\"region\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Bakragore's Burden</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">13.20.13560<br/>July 10, 2023<br/>Summer Update 2023</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"status\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Status</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Active</div>\n</div>\n</aside>\n<p><b>Bakragore's Burden</b> is a special mechanic that can be applied previously to fighting <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a>, by making sacrifices of his children's essences. Defeating Bakragore while suffering from his burden is the only way to have a chance at looting special Grand Sanguine versions of the <a href=\"#/wiki/Sanguine%20Set\">Sanguine Set</a> weapons. They are brimming with Sanguine Power Augments, which gives them an edge over the regular ones. The higher the burden stage, the higher the chance to:\n</p>\n<ul><li>loot a <a href=\"#/wiki/Sanguine%20Set\">Sanguine Set</a>'s item from <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a></li>\n<li>loot a special Grand Sanguine version of these items</li>\n<li>loot better versions of Promotion Scrolls</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Obtaining_Essences\">Obtaining Essences</span></h2>\n<p>When players fight <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a>'s progeny while under the influence of its <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore%27s%20Taints\">final taint</a>, there is a chance to drop <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Murcion\"><img alt=\"The Essence of Murcion\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/The_Essence_of_Murcion_c56c4c.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Murcion\">The Essence of Murcion</a>, <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Vemiath\"><img alt=\"The Essence of Vemiath\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/The_Essence_of_Vemiath_12ac48.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Vemiath\">The Essence of Vemiath</a>, <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Ichgahal\"><img alt=\"The Essence of Ichgahal\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/The_Essence_of_Ichgahal_ddb47a.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Ichgahal\">The Essence of Ichgahal</a>, and <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Chagorz\"><img alt=\"The Essence of Chagorz\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/The_Essence_of_Chagorz_1f67e3.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Chagorz\">The Essence of Chagorz</a>. These can be used by characters, consuming them and \"imbuing\" the character with its power. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Sacrificing_Essences\">Sacrificing Essences</span></h2>\n<p>When pulling the lever to fight <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a> while each team member bears four <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore%27s%20Taints\">Bakragore's Taints</a> plus the <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore%27s%20Taints\">final taint</a>, the team will arrive in a special antechamber, which is another lever room. There, players will have 3 minutes to prepare (<span class=\"sounds tibiatext tibiaorange\">You have only 3 minutes to prepare for the fight. To reset your sacrifice you will have to leave this room and reenter!</span>). Essence Devourers can be found in this chamber, and characters that have previously consumed essences can use these devourers to sacrifice their essences, thereby inflicting <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Bakragore's Burden</strong> upon the next fight (<span class=\"sounds tibiatext tibiaorange\">The difficulty of the upcoming battle has increased!</span>).\n</p>\n<figure class=\"thumb mw-halign-right show-info-icon\" style=\"width: 300px\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> <img alt=\"Player sacrificing the \" class=\"thumbimage\" height=\"219\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Bakragore_s_Burden_Sacrificing_Essence_of_Ichgahal_8abc51.png\" width=\"300\"/>  <figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> <svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg> <p class=\"caption\">Player sacrificing the <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Essence%20of%20Ichgahal\">The Essence of Ichgahal</a></p> </figcaption> </figure>\n<ul><li>In the antechamber, one devourer for each essence type will be available: <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Essence Devourer (Vemiath)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Essence_Devourer_Vemiath_5a0a2c.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Essence Devourer (Murcion)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Essence_Devourer_Murcion_2e43f0.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Essence Devourer (Ichgahal)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Essence_Devourer_Ichgahal_5c4ec1.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Essence Devourer (Chagorz)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Essence_Devourer_Chagorz_9312ec.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span></li>\n<li>Using them sacrifices a player's essence, charging the devourers up: <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Charged Essence Devourer (Vemiath)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Charged_Essence_Devourer_Vemiath_e34459.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Charged Essence Devourer (Murcion)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Charged_Essence_Devourer_Murcion_121a19.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Charged Essence Devourer (Ichgahal)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Charged_Essence_Devourer_Ichgahal_691c76.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span> <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Charged Essence Devourer (Chagorz)\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Charged_Essence_Devourer_Chagorz_2df0dd.gif\" width=\"64\"/></span></span></li></ul>\n<p>Sacrificed essences only inflict a burden for the next <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a> fight, and this burden is taken away at the end, regardless of the outcome of the battle (success or failure). Players need to gather and sacrifice further essences if they want to fight with the burden active again.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Outcome_of_Sacrifices\">Outcome of Sacrifices</span></h3>\n<p>Each sacrifice will increase the impact of <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Bakragore's Burden</strong>, raising both the difficulty and the rewards of the team's next fight against <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a>. There are four stages, one for each essence sacrificed:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Bakragore's Burden</th>\n<th>Stage 1</th>\n<th>Stage 2</th>\n<th>Stage 3</th>\n<th>Stage 4\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Reduced damage dealt\n</th>\n<td>10%</td>\n<td>20%</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>40%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Increased damage taken\n</th>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>75%</td>\n<td>100%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Additional loot\n</th>\n<td>5%</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>75%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Additional experience\n</th>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>45%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>225%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Additionally, for each sacrificed essence, one <a href=\"#/wiki/Elder%20Bloodjaw\">Elder Bloodjaw</a> will be replaced with one echo of a <a href=\"#/wiki/Bakragore\">Bakragore</a>'s progeny:\n</p>\n<center>\n<table>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"item-tile no-pseudoelements-container\"><div class=\"item-tile-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Chagorz\"><img alt=\"Echo of Chagorz\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Echo_of_Chagorz_9551b4.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></div><div class=\"item-tile-text\"> <a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Chagorz\">Echo of Chagorz</a></div></div></td>\n<td><div class=\"item-tile no-pseudoelements-container\"><div class=\"item-tile-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Murcion\"><img alt=\"Echo of Murcion\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Echo_of_Murcion_d10873.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></div><div class=\"item-tile-text\"> <a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Murcion\">Echo of Murcion</a></div></div></td>\n<td><div class=\"item-tile no-pseudoelements-container\"><div class=\"item-tile-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Ichgahal\"><img alt=\"Echo of Ichgahal\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Echo_of_Ichgahal_e395ca.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></div><div class=\"item-tile-text\"> <a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Ichgahal\">Echo of Ichgahal</a></div></div></td>\n<td><div class=\"item-tile no-pseudoelements-container\"><div class=\"item-tile-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Vemiath\"><img alt=\"Echo of Vemiath\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Echo_of_Vemiath_b423e2.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></div><div class=\"item-tile-text\"> <a href=\"#/wiki/Echo%20of%20Vemiath\">Echo of Vemiath</a></div></div>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</center>\n<p>After being killed, an Elder Bloodjaw will respawn in the room to replace them. These echoes are not as strong as their real versions, but each one has a separate set of skills and are still strong minions, making the fight even harder because:\n</p>\n<ul><li>they do not interact with the tracks left on the ground by players or the boss, including the <a href=\"#/wiki/Rotten%20Charge\">Rotten Charge</a></li>\n<li>they will get in the way of executing the mechanic with an Elder Bloodjaw</li>\n<li>they will not be removed from the room together with the Elder Bloodjaws</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Extracting_Essences\">Extracting Essences</span></h2>\n<p>In the same antechamber, when a character has already been imbued with an essence previously, they can click the respective <span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Essence Extractor\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Essence_Extractor_af7f6d.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span> Essence Extractor in the room to extract the essence from the character and put it back to their backpack.\n</p></div>","quests":["rotten-blood-quest"]}